  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plant Food Trees for Climate and Hunger</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UN says conserving forests and planting more trees could provide nearly one third of urgent climate mitigation needed in the next ten years. Food trees uniquely address the triple crises of global hunger, climate change, and biodiversity loss by providing food and income, carbon sequestration, and wildlife habitat, while reducing widespread deforestation driven by animal agriculture. Our Food Trees for Climate and Hunger Fund supports food tree and food forest plantings around the world.</narrative>
  </description>
